  "generated_text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of possible pairings of Chandra's bowls and glasses. Chandra has four bowls and four glasses, each of a different color (red, blue, yellow, green).\n\n1. Identify the number of choices for each color:\n   - There are 4 bowls of different colors (red, blue, yellow, green).\n   - There are 4 glasses of different colors (red, blue, yellow, green).\n\n2. Determine the number of possible pairings:\n   - For each bowl, there is exactly one glass of the same color.\n   - Therefore, for each bowl, there is only one possible glass pairing.\n\n3. Calculate the total number of pairings:\n   - Since there are 4 bowls and for each bowl there is 1 possible glass pairing, the total number of pairings is:\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 1 = 4\n   \\]\n\n4. Conclusion:\n   - The total number of possible pairings of bowls and glasses is 4.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{4}$.",
